    {
        "content": "<p>Just a small precision: in you example, <code>coherence</code> works whenever Mathlib is entirely imported</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CategoryTheory</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MonoidalCategory</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">variable</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Category</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">MonoidalCategory</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c''</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟶</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c'</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟶</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c''</span><span class=\"o\">)</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">▷</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">𝟙</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">▷</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">𝟙</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ρ_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">hom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">▷</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ρ_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">hom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ρ_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">hom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">▷</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ρ_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">hom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">monoidal</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- `coherence` now works -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">▷</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">𝟙</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">▷</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">𝟙</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ρ_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">hom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">▷</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ρ_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">hom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ρ_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">hom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">▷</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ρ_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">hom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">coherence</span>\n</code></pre></div>\n<p>Why does that make sense?</p>",
        "id": 579560440,
        "sender_full_name": "Gaëtan Serré",
        "timestamp": 1773592794
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The way to answer this is to continue to either add imports to the failing example file, or remove imports from the succeeding example file, until you find the file whose import changes the behaviour. And then copy and paste that file into your file instead of importing it and start deleting things until you find which declaration changes the behaviour. And then you've answered your own question. I could imagine that this is something you could even ask Claude Code to do nowadays.</p>",
        "id": 579570106,
        "sender_full_name": "Kevin Buzzard",
        "timestamp": 1773603011
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I am a bit surprised that there is a change of behavior due to import, so I tried looking a bit more into it. I don’t really get what changes in the environment can change the behavior of the tactics here.</p>\n<p>I also made a mistake in my previous message: the tactic that solves things made _only_ of associators and unitors is supposedly <code>pure_coherence</code>. Now, I also share your interrogation regarding the fact that we have two tactics here. <br>\nMy understanding now is that the two tactics are based on different ideas: <code>coherence</code> aggressively destructs morphisms into \"structural\" morphisms that <code>pure_coherence</code> can prove equal by lifting to the free monoidal category (which has subsingleton hom-sets) while <code>monoidal</code> and <code>bicategory</code> do not involve the free monoidal category at all, and instead do the normalization in meta code and remembers all the proofs. <a href=\"#narrow/stream/287929-mathlib4/topic/Proof.20producing.20coherence.20tactic.20for.20monoidal.20categories\">This thread</a> has explanations, and my understanding is that <code>monoidal</code> and <code>bicategory</code> are more modern, faster, and should be preferred if possible.</p>\n<p><span class=\"user-mention\" data-user-id=\"438192\">@Yuma Mizuno</span> Is that correct?<br>\nShould the old <code>coherence</code> and <code>pure_coherence</code> be deprecated?</p>",
        "id": 579571602,
        "sender_full_name": "Robin Carlier",
        "timestamp": 1773604984
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Yes, that's correct. I'm not sure about the current speed comparisons, as they may depend on kernel performance improvements. However, <code>bicategory</code> and <code>monoidal</code> are usually fast enough, so I recommend using them.</p>",
        "id": 579572051,
        "sender_full_name": "Yuma Mizuno",
        "timestamp": 1773605547
    },
    {
        "content": "<blockquote>\n<p>Should the old <code>coherence</code> and <code>pure_coherence</code> be deprecated?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I think it is good to have some explanation to avoid confusion. The PR <a href=\"https://github.com/leanprover-community/mathlib4/pull/36696\">#36696</a> added the warning message when using <code>coherence</code> and <code>pure_coherence</code>.</p>",
        "id": 579621166,
        "sender_full_name": "Yuma Mizuno",
        "timestamp": 1773642602
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thank you for these details. One small concern I have making <code>coherence</code> deprecated is that it can solve goals involving <a href=\"https://leanprover-community.github.io/mathlib4_docs/find/?pattern=CategoryTheory.monoidalComp#doc\">docs#CategoryTheory.monoidalComp</a> which <code>monoidal</code> cannot:</p>\n<div class=\"codehilite\" data-code-language=\"Lean4\"><pre><span></span><code><span class=\"kn\">import</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">Mathlib</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">open</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">CategoryTheory</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">MonoidalCategory</span>\n\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Category</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">MonoidalCategory</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c''</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">𝟙</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟶</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟶</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c''</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">MonoidalCoherence</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c'</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">λ_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">𝟙</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">hom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊗≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ρ_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">𝟙</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">hom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊗≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">coherence</span>\n\n<span class=\"sd\">/-- error: failed to unfold inst✝ -/</span>\n<span class=\"kn\">example</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"kt\">Type</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"o\">}</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">Category</span><span class=\"bp\">*</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">MonoidalCategory</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">{</span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c''</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">}</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"mi\">𝟙</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟶</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c'</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⟶</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c''</span><span class=\"o\">)</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">[</span><span class=\"n\">MonoidalCoherence</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">c'</span><span class=\"o\">]</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:</span>\n<span class=\"w\">    </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"bp\">λ_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">𝟙</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">hom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊗≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"n\">ρ_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">(</span><span class=\"mi\">𝟙</span><span class=\"bp\">_</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">C</span><span class=\"o\">))</span><span class=\"bp\">.</span><span class=\"n\">hom</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">f</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"bp\">⊗≫</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"n\">g</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"o\">:=</span><span class=\"w\"> </span><span class=\"k\">by</span>\n<span class=\"w\">  </span><span class=\"n\">monoidal</span>\n</code></pre></div>",
        "id": 579657055,
        "sender_full_name": "Gaëtan Serré",
        "timestamp": 1773654611
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Nice catch, I think this is a bug. I’ll take a look when I have some time.</p>",
        "id": 579688776,
        "sender_full_name": "Yuma Mizuno",
        "timestamp": 1773663433
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Actually, if I remember correctly, it might not be intended for users to insert <code>MonoidalCoherence</code> manually . My understanding is that this typeclass expresses that <code>c</code> and <code>c'</code> are actually related via associators and unitors. Have there been situations where you really want to use this?</p>",
        "id": 579690049,
        "sender_full_name": "Yuma Mizuno",
        "timestamp": 1773663804
    },
    {
        "content": "<p><span class=\"user-mention silent\" data-user-id=\"438192\">Yuma Mizuno</span> <a href=\"#narrow/channel/287929-mathlib4/topic/Difference.20between.20.60monoidal.60.20and.20.60coherence.60.20tactics/near/579690049\">said</a> :</p>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Actually, if I remember correctly, it might not be intended for users to insert <code>MonoidalCoherence</code> manually . My understanding is that this typeclass expresses that <code>c</code> and <code>c'</code> are actually related via associators and unitors. Have there been situations where you really want to use this?</p>\n</blockquote>\n<p>I'm really new in the category world of Lean so I have no clue if <code>MonoidalCoherence</code> should be used that way or not. In my case, I really want to use it in order to define a <code>monoidalComp</code> operation on Markov kernels (as measurable spaces and markov kernels form a monoidal category) whenever two measurable spaces are measurably equivalent (this equivalence would result to a <code>MonoidalCoherence</code> instance).</p>",
        "id": 579703033,
        "sender_full_name": "Gaëtan Serré",
        "timestamp": 1773667060
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>Thank you for explaining the background.</p>\n<p>The first step would be to define the monoidal category instance on the category of measurable space, whose morphisms are Markov kernels. Is this already available in mathlib?</p>",
        "id": 579707262,
        "sender_full_name": "Yuma Mizuno",
        "timestamp": 1773668153
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>It's not in Mathlib but Gaëtan did that in his repository (which is private for now), for Markov kernels and also for s-finite kernels. He also has a tactic that takes an equation involving <code>ProbabilityTheory.Kernel</code>, moves everything to the category with an appropriate universe, applies category tactics there, and then moves back.</p>",
        "id": 579708692,
        "sender_full_name": "Rémy Degenne",
        "timestamp": 1773668508
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>The universe lifting tactic sounds great! I have often imagined how nice it would be if such a tactic existed.</p>",
        "id": 579709389,
        "sender_full_name": "Yuma Mizuno",
        "timestamp": 1773668658
    },
    {
        "content": "<p>I didn't think such a tactic could be that interesting <span aria-label=\"sweat smile\" class=\"emoji emoji-1f605\" role=\"img\" title=\"sweat smile\">:sweat_smile:</span>. I'll have to make it more general.</p>",
        "id": 579711993,
        "sender_full_name": "Gaëtan Serré",
        "timestamp": 1773669300
    }
]